
3070 Problem:-
You are given a 0-indexed integer matrix grid and an integer k.
Return the number of submatrices that contain the top-left element of the grid, and have a sum less than or equal to k.

Example 1:
Input: grid = [[7,6,3],[6,6,1]], k = 18
Output: 4
Explanation: There are only 4 submatrices, shown in the image above, that contain the top-left element of grid, and have a sum less than or equal to 18.

Example 2:
Input: grid = [[7,2,9],[1,5,0],[2,6,6]], k = 20
Output: 6
Explanation: There are only 6 submatrices, shown in the image above, that contain the top-left element of grid, and have a sum less than or equal to 20.
 
Constraints:
m == grid.length 
n == grid[i].length
1 <= n, m <= 1000 
0 <= grid[i][j] <= 1000
1 <= k <= 109

=====================================================================================================================================================================

Solution:-
Intuition
... Every valid submatrix must start at (0,0), so we only care about top-left anchored rectangles.
... A 2D prefix sum gives us the sum of any such rectangle in O(1).
... We can build the prefix sum on the fly while scanning, and check the condition at each cell instantly.
... No need for a separate pass , compute and check in one go.

Approach:-
We use a (m+1) x (n+1) prefix sum table px, padded with zeros on the top and left to avoid boundary checks.
Take this example grid and its prefix sum table built side by side:
At each cell (i,j) in the grid, we fill px[i+1][j+1] using:
... px[i][j+1] is the sum of everything above.
... px[i+1][j] is the sum of everything to the left.
... px[i][j] is subtracted because the top-left overlap gets counted twice.
After computing px[i+1][j+1], if it is <= k, we count this submatrix.

Complexity:-
Time complexity: O(m×n) ... one pass through every cell, O(1) work each.
Space complexity: O(m×n) ... for the prefix sum table of size (m+1) x (n+1).

Code:-
class Solution {
    public int countSubmatrices(int[][] grid, int k) {
        int m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;
        int ans = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                long up = (i > 0 ? grid[i - 1][j] : 0);
                long left = (j > 0 ? grid[i][j - 1] : 0);
                long diag = (i > 0 && j > 0 ? grid[i - 1][j - 1] : 0);

                grid[i][j] = (int)(grid[i][j] + up + left - diag);

                if (grid[i][j] <= k) {
                    ans++;
                } else {
                    if (j == 0) return ans;
                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
